====================================================================================
FASTLANE EXACTNESS WITNESS v6 (INT8xINT8->INT32)
====================================================================================
We test INT8×INT8→INT32 GEMM via cublasGemmEx on realistic GPU shapes.
Formula: C(i,j) = sum_{k=0..K-1} A(i,k) * B(k,j), computed exactly in int32.
We stay inside the safe range: max |C(i,j)| << 2^31, so no int32 overflow.

--- Micro witness: M=N=K=256 (random int8 A,B) ---
C(i,j) = sum_{k=0..255} A(i,k) * B(k,j), with A,B in [-128,127].
CPU uses int64 accumulator; result stored as int32 (safe for this K).
Micro 256^3: CPU vs GPU max |diff| = 0
Micro check: all entries match exactly.

Example micro equations (CPU = GPU):
  C(0,0) = sum_{k=0..255} A(0,k)*B(k,0) = -59174  | GPU: -59174
  C(13,7) = sum_{k=0..255} A(13,k)*B(k,7) = 15001  | GPU: 15001
  C(255,42) = sum_{k=0..255} A(255,k)*B(k,42) = 107540  | GPU: 107540

--- Edge-case equations (CPU-only demos) ---
Edge 1: M=N=1, K=16, A=127, B=-128
  C(0,0) = sum_{k=0..15} 127 * (-128) = 16 * (127 * -128) = -260096
Edge 2: M=N=1, K=5120, A=127,  B=127
  C(0,0) = sum_{k=0..K-1} A_val*B_val = 5120 * (127 * 127) = 82580480
Edge 2: M=N=1, K=5120, A=127,  B=-127
  C(0,0) = sum_{k=0..K-1} A_val*B_val = 5120 * (127 * -127) = -82580480
Edge 2: M=N=1, K=5120, A=-128, B=-128
  C(0,0) = sum_{k=0..K-1} A_val*B_val = 5120 * (-128 * -128) = 83886080

--- Macro witness: M=N=K=5120, A=B=1 ---
Here A(i,k)=1 and B(k,j)=1, so:
  C(i,j) = sum_{k=0..K2-1} 1*1 = K2 = 5120 for all i,j.
We verify that every entry of the GPU result equals 5120 exactly.
Macro 5120^3 GemmEx elapsed = 4.610 ms
Copying C back to host for verification...
Macro 5120^3: expected each entry = 5120
Macro 5120^3 GPU max |C - expected| = 0
Macro check: all entries match expected value exactly.

FASTLANE INT8xINT8->INT32 exactness witness v6 finished.
